Subject: Response to Notice of Violation – Associate Certification Exam – September 26, 2026
Dear Guidewire Exam Conduct Review Committee,
I am writing in response to the Notice of Violation dated October 2, 2026, regarding my Associate Certification – InsuranceSuite Developer Proctored Exam taken on September 26, 2026.
I respectfully request that the following circumstances be considered before Guidewire finalizes its findings and the proposed remedial actions.
During the examination, the electrical socket at the location where I was seated was not working, while my laptop was running on battery. My charger itself was functioning, but I was unable to charge my laptop using the socket at my seating position. As I was concerned that my laptop could lose power and the examination could be interrupted, I needed to connect the charger to another functioning electrical socket.
For this reason, a person who was outside the room briefly entered to help me connect the charger to the alternate working socket. Their involvement was strictly limited to helping with the electrical/charging issue. They did not assist me in answering any examination questions, provide me with answers, operate my computer for the purpose of answering questions, or otherwise assist me with the examination.
I acknowledge that the examination rules required me to remain alone in the room throughout the examination. I sincerely regret that this unexpected electrical issue resulted in another person briefly entering the room. I understand how their presence may have appeared concerning from the proctor's perspective. However, I respectfully ask that the purpose, duration, and circumstances of their presence be considered, particularly in light of the fact that their involvement was limited to resolving the charging issue.
I would also like to clearly state that I did not use any artificial intelligence tool, generative AI model, automated service, external source, or other prohibited assistance to answer the examination questions. I did not share examination questions or examination content with the person who entered the room.
I am willing to provide the person's full identifying details as requested and to cooperate fully with any further questions or verification Guidewire may require. I also respectfully request that the relevant portion of the proctoring recording be reviewed to verify the circumstances, duration, and nature of the person's involvement.
Regarding examination materials, I did not intentionally photograph, screenshot, record, copy, reproduce, or distribute examination questions or content, nor did I use AI-generated material or AI interactions in connection with the examination.
I sincerely respect Guidewire's certification process, examination rules, and the importance of maintaining examination integrity. I take responsibility for the fact that the presence of another person occurred during the examination, and I regret not being able to resolve the electrical issue without creating a situation that could be interpreted as a violation of the examination rules.
However, I respectfully request that Guidewire consider the circumstances and distinguish this brief technical assistance from assistance with answering examination questions. I also respectfully request that the proposed remedial actions, including the proposed prohibition of up to five years from Guidewire training, examinations, and certifications, be reconsidered in light of these circumstances.
I am fully willing to cooperate with the Review Committee and provide any additional information or evidence that may assist in reaching an accurate decision.
Thank you for taking the time to consider my response.
Sincerely,
Prateek Kushwaha
